 ## Limits and next test
 
-The current intervention changes geometry while keeping the original graph. A useful next extension would let the visitor add a joint or revise a connection, then retain both versions for comparison. The spring damping in the automatic study is still applied per frame; compare fixed update rates before changing that separate behaviour.
+The gold joints change geometry. A turquoise collar now opens the distal end of the original left forearm connection: pick up the collar, carry it to a different gold joint and release within 0.28 m to change its neighbour. A green ring previews a valid target. Only this one endpoint is editable; the other eleven connections and all thirteen joints remain. Self-connections, duplicates and empty-space drops return to the previous attachment. They create no saved edit. The finite workspace applies to the held collar too. Both desktop carry and XRTools pickup use the same begin/release actions. A new joint remains a possible later operation. The spring damping in the automatic study is still applied per frame; compare fixed update rates before changing that separate behaviour.
 
 The private museum probe checks instantiated behaviour and selected walking routes. See the [current evidence](../../../doc/book/iterations/2026-09-21-assembly-immersion/SUMMARY.md). Headset readability, comfort, Quest performance and learner understanding remain unverified. The assembly parts are visual objects without supporting collision: walking among them does not establish a chair you can sit on or a body you can wear.
 
